## 4 ELEMENTS OF A BILL ISSUED BY HEALTHCARE ORGANIZATION

The healthcare organization shall ensure to include the following sections and details in the bill:


### 4.1 Details of Healthcare Organization

This section shall contain the following information:


#### 4.1.1 Name and Address of Healthcare Facility

- a) Full name and complete address;
- b) GSTIN;
- c) Phone number; and
- d) Email ID.

#### 4.1.2 Hospital Registration Details

- a) Registration number under the Clinical Establishments (Registration and Regulation) Act, 2010 or registration as applicable under the respective State/UT laws;
- b) License number (where applicable); and
- c) The details of accreditation (if any).

#### 4.1.3 Bill Number

A unique identifier for the bill (preferably alphanumeric).




#### 4.1.4 Bill Date and Time

Date and time of bill generation.


### 4.2 Patient Details

The following patient information shall be included in the bill:

- a) Full name of the patient;
- b) Age and gender;
- c) Patient identification number (hospital- specific);
- d) Unique Health ID (UHID);
- e) Address and contact information (phone number and email);
- f) Date and time of admission and discharge;
- g) Type of admission (inpatient, outpatient, or day-care);
- h) Emergency contact number; and
- j) GSTIN (if asked by the patient)
NOTE — Name, address and age of the patient should match the details provided in the Government issued identity document.


### 4.3 Summary of Charges

This section shall provide the heads of charges incurred during the treatment of the patient. The bill shall include, but not limited to, the following categories of charges:

- a) Room charges;
- b) Consultation fees;
- c) Procedure/Surgery charges;
- d) Investigation charges;
- e) Pharmacy/Medicines;
- f) Medical consumables and disposables;
- g) Package charges; and
- h) Miscellaneous charges.

