### 4.4 Itemization of Charges

This section shall provide a clear breakdown of all charges incurred by the patient during the treatment. The bill shall include, but not be limited to, the following categories:


#### 4.4.1 Room Charges

- a) Type of room (for example, general ward, private room and ICU);
- b) Duration of stay and corresponding dates; and
- c) Room charges per day.

#### 4.4.2 Consultation Charges

- a) Charges for doctor consultations (itemized by doctor and date); and
- b) Specialist consultation fees (where applicable).

#### 4.4.3 Procedure/Surgery Charges

- a) Name of the procedure/surgery;
- b) Surgeon fees;
- c) Anaesthesia charges;
- d) Operation theatre (OT) charges; and
- e) Other charges (specify each charge).
NOTE — Itemized breakup of procedure/surgery charges may not be applicable, if included in the package.


#### 4.4.4 Investigation Charges

- a) Name of diagnostic test in each category (for example, pathology, radiology, any other specialized test); and
- b) Charges for each test.

#### 4.4.5 Pharmacy/Medicines Charges

- a) Name of each medicine dispensed;
- b) Quantity and price of each medicine; and
- c) Batch number and expiry date of each medicine.

#### 4.4.6 Medical Consumables and Disposables

- a) Name of items (such as syringes, gloves, catheters, or any specialised medical consumable);
- b) Quantity and price of each item; and
- c) Batch number and expiry date.

#### 4.4.7 Package Charges

- a) Name of the package (with code and descriptor);
- b) Administrative charges (such as registration/admission charges); and
- c) Any other charges (specify each charge).
NOTE — Charges such as room, nursing including pharmacy, doctor’s consultation, investigation, medical consumables/disposables and administrative cost may not be applicable, if already included in the package.




#### 4.4.8 Miscellaneous Charges

Any additional charges not covered under 4.4 shall be listed clearly, specifying each charge.  An annexure may be added, if required.

