### 4.6 Additional Information

This section should include, but not limited to, the following:

- a) Modes of payment accepted by healthcare facility (for example, cash, credit/debit card, UPI and net banking);
- b) A disclaimer statement(s) such as, ‘Please verify all details before payment. For any discrepancies, contact the billing department immediately’;
- c) Status of financial counselling, specifying whether provided or not; and
- d) Names and designations of doctors involved in the patient's treatment.

## 5 FORMATTING REQUIREMENTS

To ensure readability and consistency, the following formatting requirements shall be adhered to during bill generation:

- a) Font — Use a standard, legible font (for example, Arial and Times New Roman) of size not smaller than 11 points;
- b) Layout — All charges shall be listed in a tabular format for clarity;
- c) Currency — All monetary values shall be mentioned in Indian Rupees (INR);
- d) Language — The bill shall be generated in English and/or the local regional language; and
- e) Digital Format — The bill shall be available in physical and/or digital formats.
NOTE — The bill should be generated on the letterhead of the healthcare facility and in A4 size to facilitate easy scanning.


